{"repositoryId":851782765,"availability":"available","full":"correspondMerchant/LAGO-R-Package","name":"LAGO-R-Package","description":"R package for optimizing interventions in Learn-As-you-GO (LAGO) adaptive trials","category":"Design","language":"R","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2024-09-03T17:37:42Z","updated":"2026-10-11T20:59:18Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://correspondmerchant.github.io/LAGO-R-Package/","topics":["adaptive-design","biostatistics","causal-inference","clinical-trials","implementation-trials","intervention-study","lago","r","r-package","statistics"],"demo":"https://correspondmerchant.github.io/LAGO-R-Package/live-demo.html","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:26.022Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:26.022Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:26.022Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T07:38:26.022Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["LAGOtrials is the R package that implements the Learn-As-you-GO (LAGO) method. The method is called LAGO; the package is called LAGOtrials because the name LAGO was already taken on CRAN. Throughout this documentation \"LAGO\" refers to the statistical method and \"LAGOtrials\" refers to this package. (For continuity, the functions keep the lago prefix and still return an object of class \"lago\".)","The LAGOtrials R package bridges the gap between theoretical advances in Learn-As-you-GO (LAGO) and practical applications by providing a standardized solution for:","Try it in your browser, no installation needed: the live demo runs the real LAGOtrials package client-side with webR (R compiled to WebAssembly) — edit the example and press Run. For a guided version, the playground lets you pick a bundled dataset or upload your own CSV, configure the model with sliders and toggles, and see the recommendation as interactive charts plus a copy-pasteable R snippet. The cost designer runs the visualizecost() Shiny app in the browser so you can shape each component's cost function and copy the coefficient list."],"features":["fitting the outcome models for both binary and continuous outcomes, including support for fixed center effects/center characteristics and fixed time effects,","calculating the recommended interventions based on various optimization criteria, including support for custom cost functions,","estimating the optimal intervention based on data from all stages,","calculating the 95% confidence sets for the recommended interventions and the optimal interventions."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/correspondMerchant/LAGO-R-Package/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"abc9b8261556c0819cfd97188217c91ed3d1d8530e98923a0eec85646cecdb26","extractedAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:26.194Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:26.194Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"LAGOtrials is the R package that implements the Learn-As-you-GO (LAGO) method. The method is called LAGO; the package is called LAGOtrials because the name LAGO was already taken on CRAN. Throughout this documentation \"LAGO\" refers to the statistical method and \"LAGOtrials\" refers to this package. (For continuity, the functions keep the lago prefix and still return an object of class \"lago\".)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/correspondMerchant/LAGO-R-Package/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"abc9b8261556c0819cfd97188217c91ed3d1d8530e98923a0eec85646cecdb26","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/correspondMerchant/LAGO-R-Package/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:26.194Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T20:59:18Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/correspondMerchant/LAGO-R-Package/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:26.195Z","hash":"abc9b8261556c0819cfd97188217c91ed3d1d8530e98923a0eec85646cecdb26","originalBytes":35189,"storedBytes":35189,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["cost","lago","